problem: Google Drive OAuth token file was created with default permissions before chmod hardening
approach: Created the token file atomically with O_CREAT|O_EXCL and mode 0600 before writing token contents
failed_paths:
  - Did not rely on post-write chmod because OAuth refresh tokens could be exposed during the creation window
verification:
  - cargo test
  - user-reported successful YubiKey-backed e2e test
workflow_learning: For credential persistence, verify the open/create call itself enforces private permissions rather than repairing permissions afterward
related_files:
  - src/commands/gdrive.rs
